  message: "Done in PR #3479. New IMPORT_EDGE_TYPES constant in hypergumbo_core.edge_types (imports + imports_module + imports_component); ranking and slice migrated to use it. Fixes ADR-0023 §1 case 1 silent bug (imports_component was missing from both consumer sets). Audited and unchanged: ranking._STRUCTURAL_EDGE_TYPES, slice._STRUCTURAL_EDGE_TYPES (both pure relationship-axis), io_boundary._TRACEABLE_EDGE_TYPES, taint.TAINT_CALL_EDGE_TYPES (mix axes but include 'calls', so forward-compatible through Phase 3 bridge folding). Deferrals: sketch.py has no edge-type filter (description was speculative); SCIP merger doesn't exist (the pass scip/calls.py:48 promises was never built); slice.py:612's dispatches_to compare gates on WI-kofuh-fovar dispatch-family audit. Adjacent finding for WI-tavas-voror: DEFAULT_EDGE_TYPE_WEIGHTS contains 5 emit-but-unregistered values (event_subscribes:8, crdt_publishes:3, crypto_flow:1, module_exports:1, message_dispatch:1) — same shape as the 45-triage. Tagged awaits_bakeoff_validation: behavior change is real (Vue/Svelte/Astro/React component imports now ranked/sliced as import edges) but visible only on framework-component-importing repos; DEEP cycle should confirm centrality and slice-exclusion deltas are net-positive."  # c5f5
